WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.352
Young Yang Guang was the second son of Emperor Wen of Sui; clever and studious from childhood, he read earnestly in the palace.

00:00:08.702 --> 00:00:11.606
His teachers all praised him as a fine student.

00:00:11.956 --> 00:00:20.620
To win the crown prince's position, he deliberately wore simple, plain clothes, and would not even accept gifts from others.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:30.594
He often visited his elderly father and mother, personally serving them tea and water, showing great filial piety.

00:00:30.944 --> 00:00:33.224
His parents saw this and were deeply moved.

00:00:33.574 --> 00:00:42.934
But his elder brother Yang Yong ate and drank lavishly every day, living a wasteful, extravagant life, and gradually lost their father's favor.

00:00:43.284 --> 00:00:45.492
Their father grew more and more disappointed in him.

00:00:45.842 --> 00:00:53.330
The court officials whispered among themselves too: some supported Yang Yong, while others secretly supported Yang Guang.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:01:02.824
In the end, Yang Yong was deposed, Yang Guang finally became crown prince, and a few years later he ascended the throne.

